A hidden, experimental `--member-invariants` option, requiring `--type-system-refresh`, begins member invariants (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/105). A datatype, class, trait, newtype or abstract type may declare `invariant e` members; they are parsed, printed and resolved as ghost predicates of the type, with the plan's reads restriction (an invariant depends on no mutable state), and the verifier reports them as not yet supported. A codatatype may not declare an invariant, and a program, libraries included, that declares a member invariant may not declare a codatatype. For a datatype with invariants, `raw D` names the type of all its values, and `D` the subset of them that satisfy the invariants: constructor applications and updates have type `raw D`, and the members that an invariant applies to a raw value are inferred to be raw members, in which `this` has type `raw D`. `raw` for a class, trait, newtype or abstract type, and `witness` members, are parsed but not yet supported. A `.doo` library built with the option requires it of its clients; one built without it is unchanged. Without the option, parsing, diagnostics and the generated Boogie are unchanged.
